Chapter: LirSelectorSmoke

  cites Foreword chapter Console

Section: Defs

  s-sub : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  s-sub (a) (b) = a - b

  s-add : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  s-add (a) (b) = a + b

  s-apply : (Integer, Integer -> Integer), Integer, Integer -> Integer
  s-apply (s-sub) (x) (y) = s-sub x y

  s-join : Integer -> Integer
  s-join (n) = (let v = if n > 0 then n + 1 else n - 1 in if n == 0 then v else 0) + 7

  s-tail : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  s-tail (n) (acc) = if n <= 0 then acc else s-tail (n - 1) (acc - n + 2)

 Five parameters and a division, so the allocator runs out of argument
 registers and masks RDX -- a parameter cannot keep its arrival register and
 the entry moves must be a parallel move. Emitted in order they clobber: this
 is the col-hue shape that reported red as yellow. s-clash 9 0 0 9 3 = 0.

  s-clash : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  s-clash (a) (b) (c) (d) (e) =
    if d == a then (b - c) * 6 / e
    else if d == b then (c - a) * 6 / e + 120
    else (a - b) * 6 / e + 240

  s-result : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  s-result (a) (b) = let s = a + 1 in let y = (if b > 0 then s else 100 / (b * b + 1)) in s

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (show (s-apply s-add 3 4))
    print-line-uni (show (s-join 0))
    print-line-uni (show (s-join 5))
    print-line-uni (show (s-join (-2)))
    print-line-uni (show (s-tail 5 (-2)))
    print-line-uni (show (s-tail 1 7))
    print-line-uni (show (s-clash 9 0 0 9 3))
    print-line-uni (show (s-clash 0 9 0 9 3))
    print-line-uni (show (s-clash 0 0 9 9 3))
    print-line-uni (show (s-result 5 (-2)))
    print-line-uni (show (s-result 5 3))
  end
